From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: lib: clear_user: Branch to the loop body, not to its
 padding

The loop label in __arch_clear_user() stands in front of its .p2align
directive, so every iteration branches back into the alignment padding
and runs up to three NOPs. Put the label after the directive: the
padding then runs once and the loop keeps its alignment. At the boot
clock, 20000 MiB through /dev/zero take 5.37 s instead of 7.95 s on an
A55 and 2.74 s instead of 5.30 s on an A76.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; reads from /dev/zero
return zeros (md5 of 64 MiB in 1 MiB reads and of 1000 reads of 4097
bytes).

Fixes: fe59e0358d9b ("arm64: lib: Use MOPS for usercopy routines")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/lib/clear_user.S | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/lib/clear_user.S b/arch/arm64/lib/clear_user.S
index de9a303b6ad0..143d2f75ccf2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/lib/clear_user.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/lib/clear_user.S
@@ -37,7 +37,8 @@ USER(6f, setet	[x0]!, x1!, xzr)
 	subs	x1, x1, #8
 	b.mi	2f
 
-1:	.p2align 4
+	.p2align 4
+1:
 USER(9f, sttr	xzr, [x0])
 	add	x0, x0, #8
 	subs	x1, x1, #8
